  m_text: "Line 1: using System; \u2013 This allows us to use the magical knowledge
    stored in the System Library. Without it, every spell must be fully written out.\n\nLine
    3: namespace HelloWorld \u2013 A namespace is like a spellbook that keeps your
    spells (code) organized.\n\nLine 5: class Program \u2013 A class is like a container
    of spells, holding magic that gives functionality to your program.\n\nLine 7:
    static void Main(string[] args) \u2013 The Main method is the first spell that
    is cast when the program runs. Anything inside its {} will be executed.\n\nLine
    9: Console.WriteLine(\"Hello, World!\"); \u2013 The Console.WriteLine command
    is a spell that displays words in the Console"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
