  m_text: "In C#, as in mathematics, certain operations have higher priority than
    others. This order of operations (sometimes called \u201Cprecedence\u201D) determines
    which parts of your expression get evaluated first. Here\u2019s the typical order:\n\nParentheses
    (()) \u2013 evaluate expressions inside parentheses first.\nMultiplication/Division
    (*, /, %) \u2013 next are these \u201Clevel two\u201D operations.\nAddition/Subtraction
    (+, -) \u2013 lastly, the \u201Clevel one\u201D operations."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: b0aae22f55f1cf54c8768d2a8854e9ad, type: 2}
