  m_text: 'if: The first check. If the expression in parentheses is true, the code
    block inside the braces runs.

    else if: Additional checks if the first if
    was false. You can chain multiple else if statements.

    else: The fallback
    if all previous if (and else if) conditions fail.


    These statements are
    the final layer of logic that decides which spells to cast under which circumstances.
    They rely on the boolean expressions we generate from comparison and logical
    operators. By nesting or chaining them, you can create complex behavior as needed.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
